aster than Ultron  around the set number five not  surprising that the biggest Avengers  filmed to date would not give actual  scripts to its actors given that there  were plenty of spoilers floating around  for Infinity War the Russo brothers were  not chancing any for end game wait till  you see this next one everybody talks  so no full scripts were given to any of  the cast and Holland only received his  lines it would have been strange to not  know who you were talking to until  stepping on set we could only imagine  poor Holland had to improvise his line  choices a lot number six you'd think  casting directors would take into  consideration as to whether or not the  main actress is able to work alongside  their sidekick unfortunately when they  cast Brie Larson for the role of Captain  Marvel they did not consider if she was  allergic to cats being revealed after  the fact they decided to spend more of  the budget on making the feline CGI  number seven good thing dancing wasn't  the only way to defeat Thanos because  the cast of infinity War really couldn't  do it a little music video sesh was  coordinated by some of the gas but let's  just say that some of them were really  not about it Anthony Mackey could at  least disclose that someone was doing  something right saying we shot half of  it and then people realized how bad they  were at dancing and we couldn't get  anyone else to dance Mark Ruffalo  dancing is a spectacle that everyone  should behold once in their life number  eight sometimes you gotta relieve a  little stress and prank some of your  co-stars Paul Rudd was busy filming  Ant-Man and infinity War simultaneously  so what makes all the stress better well  obviously getting pranked by Anthony  Mackey of course the real strange part  about this is the fact that Anthony  would go out of his way to do the  undisclosed pranks taking time out of  his own break to walk over to the  Ant-Man set and raise Havoc number nine  this one's a creepy Peter tingle to the  we were surprised to learn that when  Peter's arm hair stands up on his arm at  the beginning of infinity war that no  CGI was involved no they didn't tie  strings to each of his arm hairs and  pulled them up at exactly the same time  they just had someone off camera  strangely blowing on Tom's ear to make  the hair raise up we don't think we  could have kept a straight face there  number 10. Paul Bettany has seen a lot  of strange things but nothing like the  trailer town of infinity War he recalls  filming his first scene and being shown  to his trailer which was stuck somewhere  in the hundreds of trailers parked at  the studio not only is this super  unusual to have in even a blockbuster  production but it's so abnormal for an  MCU movie  number 11 some teenagers leave high  school and never come back and  unfortunately for Holland he was happy  to have left before but was now called  back for homecoming director John Watts  thought it'd be a great idea to send Tom  back to high school undercover at the  Bronx High School of Science but Tallinn  took his strange opportunity to begin  his string of giving out Secrets he told  quite literally everyone that he was  playing Spider-Man if I'm actually  Spiderman  you're nuts number 12 Holland was really  subjected to a lot of strange activity  and in this case it was the spider thong  that caused him a lot of upset to make  sure the outfit fit tightly no wonder  clothes were needed however you still  gotta make sure nothing is showing so a  thong seemed to do the trick number 13.  another unusual prank for a quite  unusual character as part of his  initiation into the MCU Tom needed a  warm welcome on the set of homecoming so  what did the crew do you for him they  replaced his chair on set with the  toilet we aren't sure if it was  functioning or not but if it was the  joke is on them he doesn't need to walk  around for the bathroom anymore number  14 for Captain America humor is very  conservative and held back but for Chris  Evans he finds the darkest of humor in  all places with all the sadness and  laying his long-lost love Peggy to rest  in Civil War Chris found this an  opportunity to send Haley Atwell a pit  from the set captioning you look pretty  hot when you're old and dead very  strange humor from America's hero number  15 when your character is supposed to be  eight foot tall You Gotta Wear antennas  for CGI work makes sense James Spader's  performance caused a lot of confusion  for the actors specifically for  Elizabeth Olsen who just couldn't focus  on the antennae because of Spader's  amazing performance she recalled The  Experience being extremely strange and  having to ignore such a dominant acting  performance on set number 16. did Chris  Pratt really get jealous over a CGI  character not so much the CGI but of the  little baby Groot statue director James  Gunn created as a stand-in for the cast  this thing was so cute that Pratt  started feeling a little upstaged by it  Gunn explained we just had this adorable  little statue standing there and we'd  get in the scene and all this stuff  would be going on and the cast would be  acting their thoughts on all of a sudden  Chris Pratt would look over at Baby  Groot and go damn it he's gonna steal  the whole movie number 17 sometimes  mocap suits can make things a little  strange on set for the other characters  with rocket being a full CGI character  that he still needed someone in a mocap  suit to interact with everyone and  seeing a Tall Sean gun get pet by the  others is strangely uncomfortable but  we're happy they went with a fuzzy  raccoon in the end number 18 yes the  Shawarma end credit scene was quite  strange and unexpected for a superhero  movie but for this group of Misfits it  became iconic but what was the oddest  aspect about this situation it was the  very subtle fact that Captain America  was really not eating like the rest this  was actually because they had shot the  scene months after